            <ArticleTitle>Genome Sequence of Bacillus velezensis S141, a New Strain of Plant Growth-Promoting Rhizobacterium Isolated from Soybean Rhizosphere.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e01312-17</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/genomeA.01312-17</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bacillus velezensis strain S141 is a plant growth-promoting rhizobacterium isolated from soybean (Glycine max) rhizosphere that enhances soybean growth, nodulation, and N2 fixation efficiency by coinoculation with Bradyrhizobium diazoefficiens USDA110. The S141 genome was identified to comprise a 3,974,582-bp-long circular DNA sequence encoding at least 3,817 proteins.</AbstractText>
